botaeng.category.energistics=Energistics
botaeng.entry.intro=Mana in the Network
botaeng.tagline.intro=Mana as an ME network holds it
botaeng.page.intro0=With &1Botania Energistics&0, an &1ME Network&0 holds &4Mana&0 alongside items and fluids. Terminals list it one mana at a time, and its tooltip says how many &1Mana Pools&0 that is.<br>It is kept in &1ME Mana Storage Cells&0: a byte holds 1000 mana, so a 1k cell holds about one pool.
botaeng.page.intro1=The buses carry mana as they carry fluids. An &1ME Export Bus&0 fills any block that takes mana: a pool, a spreader, a runic altar, a terrestrial agglomeration plate. An &1ME Import Bus&0 draws only from a pool, the one block mana comes out of.<br>An &1ME Storage Bus&0 mounts a pool as storage both ways, and anything else as a place mana can only go.
botaeng.page.intro2=A &1Mana Tablet&0, a ring or any other mana item fills and empties at a terminal the way a bucket does.<br>An &1ME Interface&0 slot holds one pool's worth.
botaeng.page.intro3=Botania's recipes ask for mana, and a pattern encoded from HEI carries it: what a runic altar, a pool or a brewery needs is written into the pattern beside the items.<br>When the pattern is pushed, the &1ME Interface&0 puts the mana into the machine along with the items.
botaeng.entry.cells=Mana Storage Cells
botaeng.tagline.cells=A pool's worth to a kilobyte
botaeng.page.cells0=Mana cells are built around their own &1ME Mana Storage Components&0, made on a &1Runic Altar&0.<br>Each takes three components of the tier below, an AE2 processor and the material of its stage of Botania: from manasteel at 1k to Gaia Spirit at 16384k.
botaeng.page.cells1=Making the components.
botaeng.page.cells2=A component goes into an &1ME Mana Cell Housing&0 to make a cell, or straight into the whole recipe.<br>A cell holds only mana, and takes an &1Inverter Card&0, a &1Sticky Card&0 and an &1Overflow Destruction Card&0.
botaeng.page.cells3=The housing.
botaeng.page.cells4=A cell from a housing.
botaeng.page.cells5=A cell in one go.
botaeng.entry.portableCells=Portable Mana Cells
botaeng.tagline.portableCells=A mana tablet on the network's terms
botaeng.page.portableCells0=A &1Portable Mana Cell&0 holds mana, and Botania takes it for a &1Mana Tablet&0: tools and armour draw on it, it charges other mana items, and a pool fills or empties it. None of that costs it AE energy.<br>It holds half as much as a cell of its tier, so a 1k one is about a tablet.
botaeng.page.portableCells1=It is charged in a &1Charger&0 and takes two &1Energy Cards&0 and an &1Overflow Destruction Card&0.<br>A few items are never filled or emptied by it or by a terminal, those whose mana is not a store, such as the &1Terra Shatterer&0.
botaeng.page.portableCells2=Making a portable cell.
botaeng.entry.fluixPool=Fluix Mana Pool
botaeng.tagline.fluixPool=A pool as deep as the network
botaeng.page.fluixPool0=The &1Fluix Mana Pool&0 holds no mana of its own: it shows the mana of the &1ME Network&0 it is on, and what goes into or out of it goes to and from the network.<br>A spreader fills the network through it; spreaders and flowers beside it draw on the network. It needs a channel, and without one reads empty and full.
botaeng.page.fluixPool1=Items dropped into it are infused as in any pool, with the network's mana.<br>Botania counts a pool's mana only up to about two billion, so a network holding more shows that much.
botaeng.page.fluixPool2=Making the pool.
botaeng.entry.buffer=ME Mana Buffer
botaeng.tagline.buffer=Somewhere to put a recipe
botaeng.page.buffer0=The &1ME Mana Buffer&0 holds 27 stacks of items and a store of mana, and does nothing with them by itself. An &1ME Interface&0 beside it puts a pattern's items and mana in; whatever is built around it takes them out.<br>To Botania it is a pool, so a spreader beside it draws its mana and a spark on it takes the mana away. Mana goes in only with a pattern.
botaeng.page.buffer1=Making the buffer.
botaeng.entry.burstTunnel=P2P Tunnel - Mana Bursts
botaeng.tagline.burstTunnel=Bursts through walls
botaeng.page.burstTunnel0=A &1P2P Tunnel&0 attuned with any &1Lens&0 or &1Mana Spreader&0 carries mana bursts. A burst that strikes the input comes out of an output whole, with its lens, colour, mana and speed, flying the way that face looks.<br>With several outputs the bursts take turns. None is split, so a lens does nothing twice.
botaeng.page.burstTunnel1=A spreader only fires at an input that has somewhere to send the burst, and waits for it as if it had flown straight. A burst that strikes the tunnel anywhere else goes out as against a wall.<br>A &1Bore Lens&0 does not break cables.
botaeng.entry.wirelessMana=Wireless Mana
botaeng.tagline.wirelessMana=The network in your pocket
botaeng.page.wirelessMana0=A &1Wireless Terminal&0 the player carries lets Botania's tools and armour draw mana from its network once the tablets in the inventory run dry; rings worn as baubles are spent after it. It never charges the network.<br>The terminal must be linked, charged and in range, as when it is opened, and each draw costs its battery a little. The &1Wireless Mana&0 switch among its settings turns this off.
